NAME
    continue - skip to the next loop iteration, or resume emulation

SYNOPSIS
    continue

DESCRIPTION
    Zero-argument shell keyword. Inside a for(1), while(1), or until
    loop, continue skips the remainder of the loop body and begins the
    next iteration (re-evaluating the loop condition or advancing to the
    next word).

    Outside any loop, continue raises a host resume request so an
    attached emulator frontend can resume execution. When no emulator is
    attached, the request has no effect.

EXAMPLES
    for i in 1 2 3; do
        if [ "$i" -eq 2 ]; then continue; fi
        echo $i
    done
    continue

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    break(1), for(1), while(1), resume(1)
